// Escape the Quarantine: English version. Keep node titles, options and jumps identical to ../es
// (a parity test enforces it). Riddles are NOT translated: TenedoR, the post-it, the cipher,
// 0426 and every name stay as in Spanish. Only the web answer differs (darkness / oscuridad).
// Conventions (commands, #tags, markup): see specs/story-engine.md
// In text lines write every ":" as "\:"; otherwise Yarn reads it as "Character: line".

title: apartamento
---
// Last answer the player typed into an answer field (#input).
<<declare $respuesta = "">>
// Number of mistakes; changes the epilogue.
<<declare $fallos = 0>>

<<scene header_police>>
<<music investigacion>>
The case #heading
Follow the clues and catch the killer before he escapes.
You can play alone or in a group\: all you need is a computer (or a phone, although it looks better on a PC) and a notepad. It should take less than 60 minutes. The clock is ticking...
You are Jane Peralta and Tony Santiago, two detectives from the Aragon police station on the trail of the infamous criminal Murderchef. Today, 23 April 2020, after a long investigation, you have made progress on the case and you have an address.
You enter a rather run-down flat, the last known location a witness has led you to. You search the place, which is quite modest; it looks like somewhere just passed through, and whoever lived here took all their personal belongings in a great hurry.
There is little more than a pile of rumpled sheets, a wilting plant and a few dusty [link key=libros]books[/link] on the shelf (they are in Spanish)... At the back of a wardrobe drawer you find a locked tablet with a sticky note on the back.
<<jump tablet_bloqueada>>
===

title: tablet_bloqueada
---
Tablet note #subheading
<<image tablet "Locked tablet with a sticky note">>
ldrcc 5 #block:postit
1 (0) #block:postit
2 (1, 1), (3, 3), (8, 2) #block:postit
3 (5, 4) #block:postit
4 (0) #block:postit
5 (1, 1), (4, 2) #block:postit
6 (0) #block:postit
7 (9, 5) #block:postit
<<hint "Get help: call your unit's hacker.">>
They tell you, quite confidently, that the password will be a real 7-letter word (in Spanish, like the books).
<<hint "Call the hacker again (hopefully they won't get fed up).">>
They suggest you start on page 5 of the CC Recipe Book (Libro de Recetas de CC), line 2...
<<hint "Tell the hacker to stop beating around the bush.">>
Despite your bad mood, they encourage you to believe in yourself. Just look carefully at how the words are written...
Enter the tablet password\: #input:respuesta #kind:password
-> Unlock
    <<if $respuesta == "TenedoR">>
        <<jump tablet>>
    <<else>>
        <<jump contrasena_incorrecta>>
    <<endif>>
===

title: contrasena_incorrecta
---
<<set $fallos = $fallos + 1>>
Wrong password. The tablet buzzes and returns to the lock screen. #outcome:fail
-> Try again
    <<jump tablet_bloqueada>>
===
